Title:
Rewiring the GCC Compilation Lifecycle for Position-Independent Modularity

Type:
Blog Post

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
- This post explains how the author “rewires” GCC (MinGW-w64) using a versioned GCC plugin/bridge to produce self-contained position-independent (PIC) Windows modules from C.  
- The problem addressed is that normal GCC/PE builds rely on imports, relocations, and external sections (e.g., `.rdata`), which breaks a strict “single `.text` / no imports / no unresolved relocs / no external data” PIC contract useful for in-memory execution.  
- The approach runs GCC twice: first to observe typed frontend information and emit a stable intermediate projection (JBIR), then again to apply deterministic transformations inside GCC (IPA + GIMPLE) before codegen.  
- Key transformations include rewriting `dllimport` calls into typed runtime API resolution, materializing literals into automatic storage, and converting global state into an explicit context propagated through the call graph.  
- It also introduces “Matrix” to externalize/log strings by hashing literals (and handling format-string prefixes) to reduce recognizable text in the module while preserving semantics for reconstruction.  
- The post is most useful for red team toolchain builders, offensive R&D, and compiler/loader researchers who need auditable, reproducible PIC artifacts and want to reason about transformations at IR/COFF level.

Technical Focus:
- GCC plugin integration points (PRE_GENERICIZE, IPA passes, GIMPLE/SSA/CFG, FINISH_UNIT)
- Import elimination via typed API resolution (hash-based DLL/API identification)
- Literal handling and string de-texting (automatic stores, Matrix hashing, format-prefix parsing)
- Global-to-context transformation (VAR_DECL capture, deterministic layout, call-graph propagation/SCC handling)
- COFF/PE validation (symbols, relocations, section hygiene; `.text`-only extraction)
- Resolver design tradeoffs (API sets/forwarders/loader delegation vs binary size)

Use Cases:
- Build Windows PIC modules suitable for reflective/in-memory loading without standard imports
- Generate `.text`-only payload components with deterministic compilation and artifact verification
- Reduce static string indicators by moving log/message text into an external reconstruction channel (Matrix)
- Experiment with different API resolution strategies to balance capability vs footprint
- Audit compiler decisions end-to-end (C → IR → COFF) for correctness and reproducibility

Keywords:
GCC plugin, MinGW-w64, compilation pipeline, GIMPLE, RTL, SSA, CFG, IPA, call graph, COFF, PE, `.text`-only, position-independent code, dllimport rewrite, import elimination, relocations, `__imp_` symbols, Windows API resolution, API hashing, FNV-1a, API sets, forwarders, reflective loading, in-memory execution, ABI (x64 RCX/R15), global state elimination, format string parsing